# Availability (`Dimension::Memory`) is ADVISORY since banshee-yk8: macOS holds
# availability near a target, so the value is stable by design and the band never
# fires — it looked like a guard and contributed nothing (measured 3.9→3.2→3.8 GB,
# never leaving GREEN, while the machine went calm→Wailing). The metric stays
# (the banshee-cot fix) as an informational reading; only the band is demoted.
# Removing `Dimension::Memory` from `is_advisory` puts it back among the banded
# memory dimensions that DRIVE the level, so a decorative availability red could
# ring a bell again — `the_banded_memory_dimensions_exclude_the_advisory_ones`
# (and `the_advisory_dimensions_are_the_display_only_ones`) fails.
file: rust/banshee-core/src/pressure/config.rs
test: the_banded_memory_dimensions_exclude_the_advisory_ones
---OLD---
            Dimension::Uptime | Dimension::Memory | Dimension::KernelFree | Dimension::Compressor
---NEW---
            Dimension::Uptime | Dimension::KernelFree | Dimension::Compressor
